     "6d652610-a89f-45ae-8b37-2b848ad21300"], Cell[
    "quotients of the hyperbolic tiling", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "954a9765-a8dc-4c58-9162-d739bdd9e8f1"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"a2ca3a36-d345-4bc0-b242-\
21a80d0b74a7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Euler characteristic ",
 StyleBox["V", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["F", "TI"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["F", "TI"],
 " = 2",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " reads the surface off the graph: 2 on the sphere, 0 on the torus, negative \
on a hyperbolic surface."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4071f179-c98e-4bd2-b66c-4098bd99a335"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every map here is ",
 StyleBox["closed",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". A line or a circle drawn on it wraps round the surface, and on a small \
map the wrap is felt within a few steps. For plane geometry use the patches \
of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrate"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrate", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c327c99d-9da5-4b81-a54b-fd4246ce5a61"],
 ", which are cut from the infinite tiling and have no wrap."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4acd385b-aeea-43bc-be1f-a2822bb11b5d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The flat tori are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["TorusTessellation"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/TorusTessellation", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "380d1b4b-e136-4717-b1e1-e020c6269fc3"],
 " graphs. The uniform maps are built with the Conway operations on a regular \
seed: rectify, truncate and their composites. Apart from the snub cube and \
the snub dodecahedron, the snub and elongated families are not built, and \
give ",
 Cell[BoxData["$Failed"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4eb130f4-ce57-47d1-a3c1-b9ad407df30f"],
 " with a message."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4abda92b-a69d-4278-bc0f-062050e0591c"],

